The port evalpaper/ext/HC-GLAD/run_method.py (HC-GLAD src @4238b20, unmodified) is imported READ-ONLY. Reused as
is: load_main_functions (arg_parse, setup_seed), load_data_functions (init_structural_encoding, get_hyperedge_index),
import_src_modules (HC, RiemannianSGD), resolve_hparams (a typed dataset has no released line -> the modal configuration
over all 12 released lines, A27 §2), unregistered_encoders, housekeeping, chunks, rng_isolated. The port's fit() (the
line-by-line copy of main.py:110-185) is copied here with its evaluation block changed (# CHANGE-TYPED):
  * data = typed_data with HC-GLAD's own init_structural_encoding (rw/dg 8) and get_hyperedge_index (triangle
    hyperedges, collated as released: the hyperedge-batching defect stays, A11/A27); setup_seed(3407 + seed) before the
    data and the model, as the port;
  * at every evaluation point each group's test set (test normals + T) is scored through main.py's shuffled test
    DataLoader (batch_size_test 9999 = one batch), unscrambled by graph id; groups 2..K from the saved RNG state S0, the
    first group last as the RNG-carrying set (RUN_NOTES §0a);
  * held-out normals: the port's freshly collated chunks (batch_size_test; and batch_size for holdout_obj), RNG-isolated.
A19/A27 memory rule: eval 4·d·N² (d = 16) = 53-90 GB per group set on typed data (< 120 GB): feasible, runs as is, on CPU
(no 40 GB A100 holds it). A run that completes with non-finite scores is A15 (A27 §1); own_code_would_crash recorded.
Own ORACLE (collector): common epoch (epoch % 5 == 0) with the max 5-seed mean test AUROC, ties lower std, then earlier
(main.py:193-199), finite in all seeds.
